I've made a new Skolelinux CD image, release 1.0 with code name Venus.
It is available from
<URL:ftp://developer.skolelinux.no/skolelinux-cd/>.  The image size is
650 MiB.

Major changes since the previous image:

  * Several improvements to the first stage installer (d-i), and more
    translations as well. (Debian)
  * Updated discover-data to detect and handle more hardware. (Petter)
  * Updated locale-config-skolelinux to support more language/regions. (Petter)
  * Corrected typo in installation script, making dhcpd restart work again.
    (Klaus Ade/Finn-Arne)
  * Improved SMB initialization, speeding up the installation. (Finn-Arne)
  * Increased /usr on several profiles and variants, to make sure there is 10%
    free after installation. (Finn-Arne)
  * Upgraded from Jave J2RE v1.3 to 1.4. (Finn-Arne)
  * Gave up trying to restart all services in the right order. Now reboots at
    the end of the installation. (Petter)
  * Security updates to: cvs (to 1.11.1p1debian-9woody7 / DSA 519-1), kdelibs
    (to 2.2.2-13.woody.10 / DSA 518-1), krb5 (to 1.2.4-5woody5 / DSA-520-1),
    kernel-image-2.4.26-1-* (fixes Kernel Crash-Exploit, desa-2004-006)
  * We probably forgot to list something.

I have testet that the CD is bootable and installable using VMWare.

A list of known bugs is available from <URL:http://bugs.skolelinux.no/>.

The following configuration for server and LTSP-server should work out
of the box:

 - Apache
 - CUPS
 - DHCP
 - DNS
 - LDAP
 - LTSP
 - NFS
 - NTP
 - SMTP/IMAP over SSL
 - SSH
 - Squid
 - Webmin
 - User administration
 - Backup
 - Host and service monitoring.
 - SMB

The following services do not work as they should:

 - cfengine (need host netgroups)
 - SQL-server (unable to install automatically)

Test it and find out more. :-)

